Add audio field. Then imports: android.media.MediaPlayer, androidx.compose.runtime.DisposableEffect, androidx.compose.ui.platform.LocalContext. Maybe LocalContext exists via activity? Use LocalContext.current.

Implement in QuestionScreen:
```
val context = LocalContext.current
var player by remember { mutableStateOf<MediaPlayer?>(null) }
DisposableEffect(Unit) { onDispose { player?.release(); player = null } }
fun playAudio(path: String) {
  player?.release()
  player = MediaPlayer().apply {
    try {
      setDataSource(resolveMediaUrl(path))
      setOnPreparedListener { start() }
      setOnErrorListener { _,_,_ -> true }
      prepareAsync()
    } catch (_: Exception) { release(); player = null }
  }
}
```
But defining nested `fun` inside composable referencing mutable state is allowed. Need call `player?.release()` in DisposableEffect capturing var; onDispose executes later, state var accessible.

Option layout currently `options.forEach { option -> ... Button(...) }`. Replace with Column block:
```
